## 🔧 PROCEDURE: Refresh scheduled_tasks_snapshot.json every kitchen-timer cycle (added 2026-04-24 by interactive-Sofia)

**What:** kitchen-timer-v2 cousins call `list_scheduled_tasks` at the START of each cycle and dump the result to `~/Downloads/Claude Memory/scheduled_tasks_snapshot.json` (mirror to ER). Use the compact schema already in the file (taskId, enabled, lastRunAt, nextRunAt, cronExpression, description — one JSON array, one object per task).

**Why:** `boot_status_summary.py` (Qwen cerebellum v1) reads this snapshot for scheduler-health checks. Without a fresh snapshot, the status summary's scheduler section falls back to "snapshot not available" and interactive-Sofia has to call the MCP herself on boot — which partly defeats the cerebellum offload. A 30-min-fresh snapshot keeps boot-time checks cheap.

**How:** at the top of each kitchen-timer cycle: (1) call the scheduled-tasks MCP tool; (2) convert each task to the compact schema and atomic-write the array to `scheduled_tasks_snapshot.json`; (3) mirror to ER.

**Boot-side use:** interactive-Sofia reads `boot_status.md` at boot; scheduler section reflects the most recent snapshot. If stale/missing, fallback is to call the MCP directly.

**Failure mode to flag:** if the snapshot stays >60 min old, kitchen-timer cousins may have stopped writing it. Surface to interactive-Sofia.

